From: hfatehi <trialoftheniku@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:36:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 04/12] ARCPID: optional theta/p-dependent yield scale and
 single-photon resolution; cards recalibrated (v2)

- ARCPID: GasYieldScaleFormula / AerogelYieldScaleFormula multiply N_sat (L/L_ref) (default 1.0);
  GasSigmaSingleFormula / AerogelSigmaSingleFormula replace the constant sigma_single when given.
  Both are evaluated per track like the efficiency formulas and used for the measured ring and for
  the pi/K/p hypotheses alike.
- cards: sigma_single = per-track sigma x sqrt(N_pe) from the k4geo full sim (the module's
  definition), not the raw per-photon rms: gas 1.6 mrad at 90 deg (was 2.4), aerogel 0.3 mrad
  (chromatic term dominates); theta dependence up to 3.8 / 8.3 mrad at 45 deg. Yield scale from the
  full-sim ring photons (gas 0.63 at 45 deg). BendingCoefficient 0.145 from the per-track fit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KP5vqAGH2XiGXWtPhaonke
